# GitHub Linguist: language statistics.
#
# `packaging/` holds build, release and platform-evidence tooling — Python
# harnesses, shell build scripts, an AppleScript UI driver, manifests and
# store assets. None of it ships: no file here appears in a release artifact.
# It is driven by the `m5-evidence-*` workflows and the release workflow.
#
# `linguist-detectable=false` is used deliberately in preference to
# `linguist-vendored` or `linguist-generated`. Those would be false: this is
# our own code, neither third-party nor generated. This attribute claims only
# that the directory should not be counted in the repository's language
# statistics, which is true — the shipped product is Rust.
#
# Stated plainly because the effect is real: `packaging/` is roughly 20% of
# the repository by line count (about 10,300 lines, mostly the three platform
# evidence harnesses). Excluding it makes the language bar describe what
# ForskScope *is*, not everything the repository *contains*. That is a
# presentation choice, made on purpose.
packaging/** linguist-detectable=false
